    "solution": "Load the Home spring and launch right onto the low landing relay. Walk from its raised position to the hanging arm, climb to its hub and cut downward to make the bridge. Read the bridge patrol, jump over it and then jump to the western tally ledge. Watch the same patrol on the return crossing before reaching the eastern mirror. Turn that mirror, drop around the upper gallery onto the low far relay, and leave left as the lift rises rather than riding into the upper dock patrol. The linked shutter completes the prepared light circuit behind you. Follow the lower conveyor to Home, load the same spring and launch left onto the widened home landing, then walk through the opened, ceiling-sealed exit.",
    "nearestExisting": "B35 supplies the reusable recoil lift, B11/B12 supply a climbing arm that becomes a bridge, and B31 supplies a changed optical return. Here two opposed lifts and their shared optical shutter trade positions together: the first landing grants ascent, the far landing completes a circuit and returns the near lift below.",
    "novelty": "The same converted bridge now has a visible patrol on both crossings. The far relay still completes the shared circuit, but its rising destination is patrolled: the useful move is to activate the lift and leave while the remote shutter finishes. The final home spring lands on a wider safe cap.",
